1
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,800
[in English] The resolution to deny
ABS-CBN's franchise application

2
00:00:08,884 --> 00:00:09,968
is hereby adopted.

3
00:00:10,052 --> 00:00:13,639
Pursuant to Section 49 of the Rules
of the House of Representatives

4
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:17,476
all House Bills and House Resolutions
relative to the grant or renewal

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,521
of the franchise application
of ABS-CBN Corporation

6
00:00:20,604 --> 00:00:21,980
are hereby laid on the table.

7
00:00:22,356 --> 00:00:24,399
[congressman] The committee secretary
is hereby directed

8
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:26,693
to inform all the authors
of the bills and resolutions...

9
00:00:26,777 --> 00:00:28,779
[in Filipino]
Why are you still watching that?

10
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:33,617
The jobs we get for our talents
are from ABS-CBN.

11
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:36,954
Where else would we
find work for them?

12
00:00:37,329 --> 00:00:38,664
This is a huge problem.

13
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:40,290
[Matthew in English]
Well, strangely enough

14
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:42,209
that's the least of our problems.

15
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,796
Maybe we can look at it
as an opportunity.

16
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,258
[in Filipino] Just think about it.

17
00:00:49,341 --> 00:00:50,342
How many decades

18
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:53,512
have the studios and networks
been running the industry?

19
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:57,182
That's why we're thinking
there's no more work for our talents.

20
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:00,435
Okay, that's valid,
but where's the opportunity there?

21
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,230
[in English] Maybe it's time
to rethink how the industry works.

22
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:06,984
[Gab in Filipino] Let's explore
new platforms for our talents.

23
00:01:07,568 --> 00:01:09,945
[in English] Maybe ABS-CBN's closure

24
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:13,115
is a signal for us to make
some changes or adjustments.

25
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:14,283
[in Filipino] Right?

26
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:15,534
It does sound like an opportunity.

27
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:18,036
But what's the point
if SAM shuts down?

28
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:24,293
[in English] Guys, I'm sorry.

29
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,003
It's not your fault.

30
00:01:26,295 --> 00:01:27,504
[in Filipino] Yeah, come on.

31
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,339
[in English]
It's not your fault, Matt.

32
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:30,924
It's your younger self's fault.

33
00:01:31,675 --> 00:01:33,635
[in Filipino]
If you didn't cheat on Gina

34
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:35,512
then we'd have money to pay for SAM.

35
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:37,097
- You're such a flirt.
- [chuckles]

36
00:01:37,389 --> 00:01:38,390
Gee, thanks.

37
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:39,766
It was a joke!

38
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:43,395
But if SAM does close

39
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:46,982
I don't think I'll move agencies.

40
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,191
Me neither.

41
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:50,360
What, do I go to Galaxy? Eww.

42
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:52,654
- I know, right?
- I'll just write a screenplay.

43
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,115
I can follow Joey to Canada.

44
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:56,491
Be an IT guy there.

45
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,035
You know IT?

46
00:01:58,452 --> 00:02:01,246
I didn't know how
to manage talents before either.

47
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,665
- But you'll stay busy, businessman.
- Right.

48
00:02:03,749 --> 00:02:05,000
[in English] No, but the thing is...

49
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:07,461
I don't want to do anything else.

50
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:10,255
And I don't want to be anywhere else.

51
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:18,180
[in Filipino]
We want to buy SAM because

52
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:21,266
we want to keep
Samuel's legacy alive.

53
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:22,351
Yeah.

54
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,770
[in English]
That name is magic in this business.

55
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,899
[in Filipino]
The bank hasn't said no yet.

56
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,192
[in English] There's still a chance.

57
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:31,777
We still have three days.

58
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,529
[in Filipino]
But one thing we have to realize

59
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:37,449
whether or not we get that loan

60
00:02:40,077 --> 00:02:41,453
things will never be the same.

61
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:45,374
[somber music]

62
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:23,912
[Helen in English]
Well, look who's here.

63
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:25,872
[in Filipino] How are you?

64
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,377
[in English] Not that I care.

65
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:33,630
[in Filipino]
That's just my standard greeting.

66
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:37,801
But I'm a decent woman,
so I'll ask you to sit.

67
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,638
[Aleta] Helen.

68
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,808
We're too old to be pulling
each other's hair, aren't we?

69
00:03:46,435 --> 00:03:47,436
[scoffs]

70
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:48,854
Well...

71
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:52,816
Don't you have questions for me?

72
00:03:54,276 --> 00:03:55,902
About me and Samuel?

73
00:03:57,279 --> 00:03:58,280
Nothing.

74
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,115
I no longer care about that.

75
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:02,284
[in English] It's all in the past.

76
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:06,329
Exactly.

77
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:14,838
[in Filipino]
You can't be serious, Aleta.

78
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:20,427
[in English] You know I would not
take your money for anything.

79
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:25,557
And I would not do anything
to make you feel better.

80
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,686
[in Filipino]
That document may have my signature

81
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,981
but it's also for Matthew

82
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:36,151
Andrea, and Gabriel too.

83
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,323
[in English] Like I said,
I would not do anything

84
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:43,325
to make you feel better.

85
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,580
Then do it for Samuel.

86
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:52,167
Do it in his memory.

87
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:56,338
All the memories I have with Samuel

88
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,465
include you.

89
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:02,886
[in Filipino]
Why would I want to relive that?

90
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,975
It was Samuel who chose to leave me.

91
00:05:09,935 --> 00:05:11,186
[in English] I don't believe you.

92
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:15,899
He would've left me for you
the minute he had a chance.

93
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,318
[in Filipino] And he had his chances.

94
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:20,612
But he didn't leave you.

95
00:05:22,906 --> 00:05:26,952
It's because he loved you,
that's why he stayed.

96
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:31,414
But above you and me

97
00:05:32,666 --> 00:05:34,376
he loved SAM more.

98
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:36,336
Compared to that...

99
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,173
neither of us could win.

100
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:43,885
[in English]
I can give you my answer right now.

101
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:45,887
No.

102
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,641
[in Filipino]
When you realize the truth...

103
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,977
[in English]
I told you I would not do anything

104
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:53,895
to make you feel better.

105
00:05:57,274 --> 00:06:00,026
[thrilling music]

106
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,362
[overlapping dialogue]

107
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,161
[overlapping dialogue continues]

108
00:06:17,627 --> 00:06:20,255
[staff 1] Move fast.
We have a lot of stuff to move.

109
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,011
[staff 2] Careful. This might fall.

110
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,596
[staff 3] Hey, wait!

111
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:32,350
[indistinct chatter]

112
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:42,277
Come on!

113
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,904
Why is this so heavy?

114
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:47,490
Um, guys.

115
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:53,079
This situation is temporary.

116
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:58,376
The old office badly needs
extensive renovation.

117
00:06:59,628 --> 00:07:02,172
[Matthew in English] Every little bit
that we can save will go a long way.

118
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:05,759
That's why we all have
to share this space.

119
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,142
[in Filipino]
Gab and I stay down here?

120
00:07:15,727 --> 00:07:17,187
Am I back to being a junior manager?

121
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,316
Are we redesigning interiors now?

122
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:23,985
[frustrated sigh]

123
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:25,153
Is there coffee in this dump?

124
00:07:25,862 --> 00:07:27,197
Coming, ma'am!

125
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:28,907
Camille!

126
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:33,787
[Andrea] Tell Deo
to move our tables up there.

127
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:35,372
- Now.
- [Camille] Okay, ma'am.

128
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,501
[Matthew] Still no word
from the bank.

129
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:43,630
Unfortunately, we were not able
to raise the money on our own.

130
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:45,924
But SAM has a good reputation.

131
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,134
Let's hope

132
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,303
the bank sees that.

133
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:53,264
So this means we keep on working?

134
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:56,142
What do we do while waiting?

135
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:58,603
If we get new management,
will you stay?

136
00:07:58,687 --> 00:08:00,313
To answer everyone's question...

137
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:03,775
What do we do?
The truth is, we don't know.

138
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:04,859
Guys...

139
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:07,946
[coffee machine whirring loudly]

140
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,158
God, forget the coffee.

141
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:14,035
I said, forget the coffee!

142
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,162
I'm sorry!

143
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,790
Goodness, I can't.

144
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:21,751
If SAM must go down

145
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:24,963
and the Screen Spirit Awards

146
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:27,966
is truly our last, our biggest event

147
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:30,301
then we must go out with a bang!

148
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:31,469
- Right?
- [Camille] With a bang!

149
00:08:31,553 --> 00:08:32,846
Yes, with a bang!

150
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:38,184
Wow, how beautiful!

151
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:39,769
You'll be a head-turner, babe!

152
00:08:39,853 --> 00:08:41,354
[Noemi] We all have to look good.

153
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:44,149
They can't know our struggles.

154
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,818
Win or lose,
whether SAM closes or not

155
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:48,778
we will be our grandest.

156
00:08:49,446 --> 00:08:50,864
Slickest!

157
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,365
[employee 1] The freshest.

158
00:08:52,449 --> 00:08:53,825
Most debonair.

159
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:55,285
Instagram-ready.

160
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:56,536
Best dressed!

161
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:59,831
I spent the best years
of my life in Shine.

162
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,250
We are Shine!

163
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,044
- [Matthew] We are Shine!
- [Camille] We are Shine!

164
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:05,211
We are Shine!

165
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:06,838
- We are Shine!
- [Camille] Bang!

166
00:09:07,839 --> 00:09:08,882
I'll go first!

167
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:09,966
Okay, fine.

168
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:11,301
- Miss Andrea!
- I'll go next, okay?

169
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:12,677
- Okay, Sir Matthew.
- Miss Andrea!

170
00:09:12,761 --> 00:09:14,054
- Yeah?
- Phone for you.

171
00:09:14,137 --> 00:09:15,638
- At your office.
- I'll be back.

172
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,062
Andrea here.

173
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:25,023
Hey, get these flowers off my desk.

174
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,107
[employee 2] Huh?

175
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,235
- These flowers! Are you deaf?
- [employee 2] Right away, ma'am!

176
00:09:29,319 --> 00:09:30,820
[Rina over phone speaker] I miss you.

177
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,406
I miss your smile.

178
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:36,326
I miss your smell.

179
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:41,289
I feel so alone, Andrea.

180
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:44,042
I wish you were here.

181
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:46,044
Can we talk?

182
00:09:46,628 --> 00:09:48,088
Hello, Rina, yeah.

183
00:09:48,755 --> 00:09:49,756
What?

184
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:51,883
[Chin] Hey, let's go there!

185
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:53,426
[Camille] Noemi, let's go.

186
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:57,639
[Andrea] Hello, yeah, Rina, um...
Hi...

187
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,186
[sobs, sniffles]

188
00:10:10,819 --> 00:10:11,820
[exhales sharply]

189
00:10:21,955 --> 00:10:22,956
[Matthew] What happened?

190
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:30,505
[whimpers]

191
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,675
Rina just called.

192
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:39,514
I already have a lot on my mind...

193
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:40,682
[quivers]

194
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:47,438
...and now she jumps in
and complicates everything.

195
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:54,654
[sobs]

196
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:56,114
We lost Samuel.

197
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,783
We're losing our talents.

198
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:00,785
We're about to lose SAM.

199
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:03,288
And with my mom's situation...

200
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:11,588
And we're all working
in this cramped office.

201
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:19,179
I don't even know where to start...

202
00:11:19,971 --> 00:11:24,267
to fix everything,
and then she calls.

203
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:28,354
So you miss Rina?

204
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,523
No! [sniffles]

205
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:31,858
You don't miss Rina?

206
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:32,942
Yes...

207
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:34,944
No!

208
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,487
I don't...

209
00:11:36,988 --> 00:11:38,573
I don't know.

210
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,751
[Zsa Zsa] ...the whale sharks.

211
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:50,877
Are you ready?

212
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,086
Let's go!

213
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:54,547
[lively music]

214
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:55,840
We're so busy with work

215
00:11:55,924 --> 00:11:58,051
that we don't have time
for boyfriends.

216
00:11:58,134 --> 00:11:59,177
Is it yummy?

217
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,054
Yes!

218
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:05,808
[lively music continues]

219
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:24,911
[Brandon cheering]

220
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:28,706
We have a lot on our plate,
literally!

221
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:33,836
I hope you enjoyed watching!

222
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,797
Please subscribe, okay?

223
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:42,387
This is really high!

224
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,682
I'm going to jump!

225
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,767
Here we go! [chuckles]

226
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:59,112
[squeals]

227
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:01,322
- Success!
- I told you so!

228
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:02,490
I feel like crying.

229
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:03,866
This is excellent! Great job!

230
00:13:04,784 --> 00:13:06,035
Uh...

231
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:07,662
But what's it for?

232
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:09,163
Um...

233
00:13:09,247 --> 00:13:12,417
This is a preview
of what's in store for our talents.

234
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,836
Yes, we're working
on the social media presence

235
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,254
- of our talents.
- True!

236
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:17,880
You always say, Sir Gab

237
00:13:17,964 --> 00:13:20,341
"This is the future
of entertainment!"

238
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:24,345
Now our content
can be seen everywhere

239
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,681
so the SAM community is growing!

240
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,434
That's right,
and with this kind of slate...

241
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:32,895
Believe me, we're projecting
around a hundred thousand

242
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:34,689
- up to millions of followers!
- [Sofie] Millions!

243
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:37,483
- Millions!
- Yes! There's more! Gosh.

244
00:13:37,567 --> 00:13:38,693
We're seeing dozens of offers

245
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:42,322
from lots of brands
for all our talents!

246
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:45,074
That's on top of TV and other media!

247
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:46,159
Take note!

248
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,996
[in English] So who thought of this?

249
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:53,291
[in Filipino]
Chin started it with Rob and Kiray.

250
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:55,752
[Gab] Good job, Chin.

251
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:58,338
[Camille] Then we built on it
with Noemi's vision.

252
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:00,256
[Matthew] But, you know

253
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:05,887
some of these talents
might not be here anymore...

254
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,222
- Then we'll find more!
- There's a lot, Sit Matthew.

255
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:10,224
- And we'll make more content!
- Yes.

256
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,726
- We can do this!
- Yes!

257
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,603
Correct!

258
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:15,897
[sighs]

259
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,857
Wonderful job, guys!

260
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,317
- [squeals]
- Good work, good work.

261
00:14:21,444 --> 00:14:24,989
- This is going to be viral.
- My gosh.

262
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,283
- [Daisy] Your nails are pretty!
- [Sofie] Right?

263
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:29,535
- [Daisy] Like candles.
- [Deo] Uh...

264
00:14:29,619 --> 00:14:30,620
Ms. Sofie.

265
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:33,748
Can you type and print this for me?

266
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:34,832
Ah!

267
00:14:34,916 --> 00:14:36,751
Sure thing.
This is a quick-dry polish, anyway.

268
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:37,835
Leave it here.

269
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:41,214
Hm...

270
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:45,134
Hey.

271
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:47,762
Are you serious? Why?

272
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:50,014
[exhales sharply]

273
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:54,602
I can't do this anymore.

274
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:56,896
- [Sofie] What?
- He's being an idiot.

275
00:14:57,313 --> 00:15:00,191
You shouldn't have fixed things

276
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,776
if you're going to leave anyway.

277
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:09,826
- I can't do this anymore.
- [Sofie] I know.

278
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:13,996
If we can't stop you, go to Admin

279
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,123
and get me an envelope for this

280
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:17,500
so once I print it,
I'll hand it in there.

281
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:21,671
You're not going to cry?

282
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,131
We're good.

283
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:26,217
What are your plans?
Why are you leaving?

284
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,344
[Daisy] What will you do
when you leave SAM?

285
00:15:28,428 --> 00:15:29,804
No idea. What are you guys doing?

286
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:32,849
I'm already doing it.

287
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,017
And Sofie is going to be an actress.

288
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:36,102
[Sofie] Right.

289
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:38,771
I have so many side hustles
here at SAM.

290
00:15:38,855 --> 00:15:40,398
I'm sure I'll live.

291
00:15:40,982 --> 00:15:42,984
Plus there are loans I've given out.

292
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:46,571
- Wait, you still owe me.
- Envelope.

293
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:50,283
What's up with him?

294
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:51,951
What's he up to?

295
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:53,453
Not in here.

296
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,037
- No, sir.
- Is this SAM?

297
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,374
Not here either.

298
00:15:58,458 --> 00:15:59,876
- Not here either?
- Yes, sir.

299
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:02,462
We've been looking all over.

300
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,430
- Hey, Deo!
- Sir Monsour!

301
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:15,183
We've been looking for you guys!

302
00:16:15,266 --> 00:16:16,267
We're over here, sir.

303
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,144
- Is Andrea there?
- Yes, sir, she's inside.

304
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,770
We couldn't find her.

305
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,856
- I'll take you to her.
- Come on.

306
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:23,191
- Hello.
- [Gab] Mon, good to see you!

307
00:16:23,274 --> 00:16:24,484
[Monsour] Hi, Gab, how are you?

308
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:26,194
- Hi, everybody.
- [employee 1] Sir Mon.

309
00:16:26,277 --> 00:16:27,320
[Monsour] Hello.

310
00:16:28,029 --> 00:16:29,030
Where's Andrea?

311
00:16:30,281 --> 00:16:31,282
Andrea?

312
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:32,867
- [Andrea] Mon?
- Andrea?

313
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:33,993
Mon!

314
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:35,828
- Hey, I'm here!
- [Monsour] Oh!

315
00:16:35,912 --> 00:16:37,997
- [Andrea] Hi! Yeah.
- [Monsour] Andrea, hi.

316
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,832
- Sorry about the mess.
- I didn't see you there.

317
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:40,958
Sorry.

318
00:16:41,042 --> 00:16:43,544
We're just trying something new here.

319
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:45,129
So what can I do for you?

320
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:47,590
I just wanted to let you know...

321
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:50,426
- Because...
- What?

322
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,929
[coffee machine whirring loudly]

323
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,555
I want you to hear it from me.

324
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:58,851
- [muffled dialogue]
- [whirring continues]

325
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:02,980
Wait.

326
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:04,774
Hey.

327
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:07,527
Stop it, for crying out loud!

328
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:10,780
Get coconut juice!
No coffee from now on, okay!

329
00:17:11,614 --> 00:17:13,366
Okay, sorry.

330
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,536
Again, please.

331
00:17:16,619 --> 00:17:19,705
I came here to tell you personally

332
00:17:20,248 --> 00:17:21,541
to let you know

333
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:24,210
that Director Lav Diaz and I
have decided

334
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:26,254
to shelve the film.

335
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,340
[Monsour]
We're not going to finish it.

336
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,175
[Andrea] But...

337
00:17:32,093 --> 00:17:35,846
But you've already spent
eight million on it, right?

338
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:37,932
Uh... That's true.

339
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,560
- Yeah, I'm just so busy...
- Sorry I missed your call...

340
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:42,770
- I'm so unbelievably busy, yes!
- Really busy, sorry.

341
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,022
So for now

342
00:17:45,106 --> 00:17:48,192
I really want a time out
from all this.

343
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:52,738
Well... Yeah, I understand.

344
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:56,242
Um, well, you still have
contracts with us, but...

345
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,244
but that can be discussed.

346
00:17:58,327 --> 00:17:59,370
Why?

347
00:18:00,288 --> 00:18:01,622
I'm not leaving SAM.

348
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,207
- You're not?
- [Monsour] No!

349
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:07,253
Come on.
I've decided that I want to run.

350
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,088
Where are you going?

351
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:12,466
[chuckles]
No, I want to run for mayor.

352
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:15,511
- [Andrea] Oh, politics. Okay.
- [Monsour] Yes.

353
00:18:15,595 --> 00:18:20,308
I really want to serve my countrymen.

354
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:23,311
If I can't be a hero
in the movies anymore

355
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:27,440
maybe I can be a hero in real life.

356
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:28,941
- [Andrea] Of course.
- [Monsour] Right?

357
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,485
It's a new adventure,
and I can do it.

358
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:33,154
Of course, you can. We can do this!

359
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:34,655
- [cell phone vibrates]
- My question is

360
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:38,117
can Shine help me with this?

361
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:40,745
Uh...

362
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:44,165
Do you have a running mate in mind?

363
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,125
Hm?

364
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:48,544
Running mate?

365
00:18:57,261 --> 00:19:00,264
[Andrea] To make things easier,
you should each create a story.

366
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:02,350
When you're done, pass it on to me.

367
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:06,312
So it's easier for me
to narrow down what we'll do.

368
00:19:06,771 --> 00:19:09,857
And then, for the options,
start from the top.

369
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:11,984
- I'll know what to include.
- Excuse me...

370
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:13,069
Yes?

371
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:15,404
Can I talk to Camille for a second?

372
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:16,989
Sure, we're all done.

373
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:20,868
For me?

374
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,706
It's beautiful!

375
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:31,796
Can I pull this off?

376
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:32,880
Of course you can!

377
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:33,964
- Yes, you can.
- You like it?

378
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:35,800
Thank you.

379
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:38,135
Let me ask you.

380
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:39,845
Do you like?

381
00:19:40,388 --> 00:19:42,473
- Looks good!
- No...

382
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:43,808
[chuckles]

383
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:45,768
I mean, do you like it?

384
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:50,398
- [Camille] Thank you!
- Aww...

385
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:54,527
[Sofie] Oh, my god, Rob! You're here!

386
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:58,614
Everyone, Rob!
Our Best Actor nominee!

387
00:19:58,698 --> 00:20:01,200
[all cheering]

388
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:04,453
Thank you so much!

389
00:20:04,537 --> 00:20:06,080
This is my mom.

390
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,832
My beautiful mother.

391
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:11,502
Sir Gab, I brought my mom.

392
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:13,796
- Congrats.
- Congratulations.

393
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:14,880
- Thank you!
- Hi!

394
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:16,549
Chin!

395
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:20,302
- How are you?
- I'm fine.

396
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:24,598
- How about you? I'm proud of you!
- Well, you know...

397
00:20:24,682 --> 00:20:26,851
[cell phone ringing]

398
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:27,935
Oh, shoot.

399
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:29,478
Matt.

400
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,240
Good morning, Mr. Villacin.

401
00:20:42,283 --> 00:20:43,284
How can I help you?

402
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:44,452
[over speaker phone] It's Frank.

403
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:46,537
Following up on our new partnership.

404
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:49,749
Partnership?

405
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,918
[Frank] Whatever you want to call it.

406
00:20:53,836 --> 00:20:56,422
I don't care for labels.

407
00:20:56,505 --> 00:21:00,217
What I want is that you work with me.

408
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,888
One, I can guarantee your bank loan.

409
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:09,143
Two, you get a permanent client
in yours truly.

410
00:21:13,481 --> 00:21:15,399
Uh... Frank?

411
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:20,029
We're not interested in that kind
of business relationship.

412
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:23,449
You have no other options.

413
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:26,911
We all know that SAM
is in dire straits right now.

414
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:30,331
Allow me to help you.

415
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:31,749
Um...

416
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:32,833
How?

417
00:21:33,584 --> 00:21:36,337
Join me and my team

418
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,674
and I will be your biggest asset.

419
00:21:41,342 --> 00:21:45,346
My name is gold
in the banking community.

420
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:48,390
You'll get your loan

421
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,143
and your problems will disappear.

422
00:21:51,519 --> 00:21:52,520
It's that simple.

423
00:21:52,603 --> 00:21:53,604
Oh!

424
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:54,980
Thank you.

425
00:21:55,231 --> 00:21:58,275
But we'll have to tell this
to Gab first, okay?

426
00:21:58,359 --> 00:22:00,361
Yeah. It's okay.

427
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:03,781
But don't make me wait too long.

428
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,658
I've waited long enough

429
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,326
and I don't like that.

430
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:08,661
Oh!

431
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:12,039
No worries.
It will just take a few minutes.

432
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:13,624
I'll call you back, okay?

433
00:22:16,252 --> 00:22:17,253
[cell phone beeps]

434
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:23,092
Hey, Gab?

435
00:22:28,222 --> 00:22:29,223
Chin!

436
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,269
[grunts] Thank you!

437
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,063
You're welcome, of course. Always.

438
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:37,147
For everything.

439
00:22:40,234 --> 00:22:41,318
But...

440
00:22:42,695 --> 00:22:43,696
are you really okay?

441
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:45,656
Yes, I am.

442
00:22:47,116 --> 00:22:48,325
I'm really okay.

443
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:49,994
Proud of you.

444
00:22:51,579 --> 00:22:53,455
Um, Rob?

445
00:22:53,539 --> 00:22:54,999
- [Rob] Yes?
- Can you...

446
00:22:55,541 --> 00:22:56,542
Can you come here, please?

447
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:57,835
Go.

448
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:00,629
[clears throat]

449
00:23:03,299 --> 00:23:04,300
[Frank over phone] Hello, SAM.

450
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:06,719
What's wrong with your head, Andrea?

451
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:10,681
[chuckles] Mr. Villacin,
it's been that way since you called.

452
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:13,475
Uh...

453
00:23:14,852 --> 00:23:17,229
Mr. Villacin, hello. This is Gabriel.

454
00:23:18,439 --> 00:23:20,316
[Frank in Filipino]
I told you, call me Frank.

455
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:23,235
Uh...

456
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:25,362
We would've wanted
to talk to you in person

457
00:23:25,446 --> 00:23:27,406
but we're kind of busy at the moment.

458
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,658
So this will do.

459
00:23:29,742 --> 00:23:30,743
[Frank] You're busy?

460
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:32,536
Busy closing shop?

461
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:35,497
Just kidding.

462
00:23:36,290 --> 00:23:39,376
I know you guys
are still the best in the business

463
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:42,338
so I'll stay with you
as long as you need me.

464
00:23:44,757 --> 00:23:45,758
About that...

465
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:49,386
We talked about your proposal.

466
00:23:50,054 --> 00:23:53,182
And we've decided

467
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:57,978
that the best way
to go about it is to...

468
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,105
not go about it.

469
00:24:01,899 --> 00:24:03,025
We respectfully decline.

470
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:05,110
No, let me rephrase that.

471
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:08,864
- [Gab] We are rejecting your offer.
- [frustrated exhale]

472
00:24:08,948 --> 00:24:10,366
[grunts]

473
00:24:11,742 --> 00:24:12,743
What did you say?

474
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:15,496
Okay.

475
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:18,582
Now you listen to me.

476
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:22,252
You need me!

477
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:25,172
You're making a big mistake!

478
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,429
Someone important to me once said

479
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:34,765
that I should listen to my heart

480
00:24:36,183 --> 00:24:40,980
and listen to my gut feel.

481
00:24:42,398 --> 00:24:44,400
And you know what? Right now...

482
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,860
our gut tells us

483
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:49,738
we have everything
we need right here.

484
00:24:50,781 --> 00:24:51,824
Frank.

485
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:54,660
[in English] Are you sure?

486
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:57,663
I will never make this offer again.

487
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:00,541
We're actually quite sure,
Mr. Villacin.

488
00:25:00,874 --> 00:25:02,001
Thank you.

489
00:25:05,587 --> 00:25:06,588
Okay.

490
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:10,384
Rob, I'm so sorry.

491
00:25:11,135 --> 00:25:12,594
I just wanted you to hear the call.

492
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:15,597
[in Filipino] It's okay.

493
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:18,517
I know you wouldn't do that to me.

494
00:25:20,269 --> 00:25:21,270
And, Ms. Andrea?

495
00:25:22,438 --> 00:25:23,439
That's me.

496
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:25,941
I'm the one who's staying.

497
00:25:27,526 --> 00:25:29,445
[in English] I will stay for as long
as you want me.

498
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:31,989
Thank you.

499
00:25:32,990 --> 00:25:34,867
- Oh, Chin?
- [Chin] Mm-hm?

500
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:37,077
- It's time for Rob's makeup.
- Okay. Let's go.

501
00:25:38,162 --> 00:25:39,163
Oh!

502
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:40,998
I almost forgot.

503
00:25:46,879 --> 00:25:47,880
What's this?

504
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:51,633
[suspenseful music]

505
00:26:06,190 --> 00:26:07,191
Think of it as an eraser.

506
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:11,111
You can watch it tomorrow.

507
00:26:20,079 --> 00:26:21,080
[sighs]

508
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:23,957
Yuni!

509
00:26:25,209 --> 00:26:27,711
Call Helen Mendiola. Now!

510
00:26:29,004 --> 00:26:31,840
The entertainment industry
is so powerful.

511
00:26:33,217 --> 00:26:35,010
People watch our every move.

512
00:26:36,470 --> 00:26:40,057
They worship our artists and talents.

513
00:26:41,809 --> 00:26:44,436
We can control what they wear

514
00:26:45,062 --> 00:26:46,772
where they go on holiday

515
00:26:47,648 --> 00:26:49,233
even how they think.

516
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:53,946
But people in this industry
don't realize

517
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:58,242
that power comes with responsibility.

518
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:00,994
Just think about it.

519
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:03,455
Imagine what we can do

520
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:06,834
if we use that power for good

521
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:09,837
instead of just wasting it.

522
00:27:16,051 --> 00:27:17,678
- [clears throat]
- Thanks.

523
00:27:19,388 --> 00:27:21,390
So, any news?

524
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:23,600
A lot.

525
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:26,770
The bank rejected our application.

526
00:27:27,521 --> 00:27:28,605
They won't give us the loan.

527
00:27:30,691 --> 00:27:32,442
[sighs]

528
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:35,320
Darn that Frank Villacin.

529
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:41,118
[in English] You know...

530
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:42,870
I'm not sure it's Frank.

531
00:27:43,704 --> 00:27:44,705
[in Filipino] He's right.

532
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:47,207
It's a risky business.

533
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:49,668
When you consider the state we're in

534
00:27:51,003 --> 00:27:52,462
who would risk giving us a loan?

535
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,135
Anyway, uh...

536
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:01,305
it's too late now.

537
00:28:08,729 --> 00:28:09,771
So I guess that's it.

538
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:13,025
She's not saying who it is.

539
00:28:13,984 --> 00:28:15,527
But she'll be making
an announcement soon.

540
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:17,905
I bet it's Paul Amir.

541
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:21,825
What do we do now?

542
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:26,121
[groans]

543
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:29,583
[somber music]

544
00:28:31,168 --> 00:28:34,171
[indistinct chatter]

545
00:28:44,348 --> 00:28:47,935
[inaudible dialogue]

546
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:18,632
- Sir Gab!
- Yo, Sir Gab!

547
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,300
Thank you!

548
00:29:23,387 --> 00:29:24,388
Pa!

549
00:29:25,264 --> 00:29:26,682
[Camille] Thank you!

550
00:29:27,057 --> 00:29:28,976
Ms. Andrea, thank you!

551
00:29:29,059 --> 00:29:30,060
Thank you!

552
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:34,314
For Ms. Andrea?

553
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,233
Ms. Andrea!

554
00:29:37,693 --> 00:29:38,819
Someone sent this.

555
00:29:38,902 --> 00:29:40,904
- [chuckles]
- Oh! Thank you.

556
00:29:47,077 --> 00:29:48,245
It's from Rina.

557
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:49,329
- Ah!
- Oh!

558
00:29:49,413 --> 00:29:50,706
She says I should use it later.

559
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:55,127
Don't forget! Joey will call later!

560
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:57,254
Okay, thanks! I'll take care of it.

561
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:04,261
[in English] Did we fail?

562
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:15,272
- [laughter]
- [indistinct chatter]

563
00:30:16,732 --> 00:30:17,733
Matty?

564
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,401
I don't think we failed.

565
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:20,944
Really?

566
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:23,947
I don't think so.

567
00:30:26,366 --> 00:30:27,367
[Andrea] You know what?

568
00:30:27,701 --> 00:30:28,702
[in Filipino] I think

569
00:30:29,911 --> 00:30:31,663
let's not tell them anything yet.

570
00:30:33,498 --> 00:30:34,499
[in English] Well, I'm happy.

571
00:30:34,875 --> 00:30:37,210
♪ ... all alone ♪

572
00:30:37,294 --> 00:30:39,421
[in Filipino]
But I'd be happier if we owned SAM.

573
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:42,007
[chuckles]

574
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:44,176
♪ ... all alone ♪

575
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:46,136
[in English]
You did your best, Matty.

576
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:49,681
We all did.

577
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,059
Yeah.

578
00:30:52,142 --> 00:30:54,644
♪ I don't feel all right being one ♪

579
00:30:54,728 --> 00:30:56,646
♪ All alone from beginning to end ♪

580
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:57,981
[Camille] Picture!
Let's take pictures!

581
00:30:58,607 --> 00:31:02,027
♪ Oh, can anyone lend me a friend? ♪

582
00:31:02,778 --> 00:31:04,613
♪ To help me around the bend ♪

583
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:06,865
[employee 1] Three, two, one!

584
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:08,283
[camera shutter clicks]

585
00:31:09,785 --> 00:31:12,496
♪ A friend to the very end ♪

586
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:16,291
♪ 'Cause I don't feel all right
Being one ♪

587
00:31:16,375 --> 00:31:17,459
Hey, let's go!

588
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:20,921
♪ No, I don't feel all right
Being one ♪

589
00:31:21,004 --> 00:31:23,256
♪ I'll be a friend to you ♪

590
00:31:23,340 --> 00:31:24,966
Pa, wait,
let's take a picture together.

591
00:31:25,050 --> 00:31:27,177
♪ It's great fun when we're two ♪

592
00:31:27,260 --> 00:31:28,678
♪ Not just you all alone ♪

593
00:31:28,762 --> 00:31:29,930
Where's Gab?

594
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:31,014
Oh, no!

595
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:33,725
Gab? Let's go!

596
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:36,978
♪ How about singing a little tune? ♪

597
00:31:38,522 --> 00:31:41,066
♪ Blending in harmony too ♪

598
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:45,487
♪ Singing like we were made
For each other, together ♪

599
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:50,117
♪ It's like we do it all the time ♪

600
00:31:52,327 --> 00:31:56,373
♪ It's like we do it all the time ♪

601
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:57,457
Oops!

602
00:31:57,541 --> 00:32:00,168
- Wow, what was that?
- [giggles]

603
00:32:00,252 --> 00:32:01,711
Sorry, we're still here.

604
00:32:01,795 --> 00:32:02,921
Really sorry.

605
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:04,631
We thought you were all gone.

606
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:05,882
- [Daisy] Goodness.
- Sir Gab.

607
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:07,759
- We didn't see a thing!
- You dropped this.

608
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:08,927
- Thank you!
- [Daisy] Nothing!

609
00:32:09,010 --> 00:32:11,054
- I have vertigo.
- [chuckles]

610
00:32:12,097 --> 00:32:13,098
This is your fault.

611
00:32:13,181 --> 00:32:15,350
[thrilling music]

612
00:32:15,434 --> 00:32:18,645
[crowd cheering]

613
00:32:20,981 --> 00:32:24,317
[indistinct chatter]

614
00:32:33,410 --> 00:32:34,536
Here they come!

615
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:37,706
The big stars are starting to arrive!

616
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:41,126
[vlogger] We'll soon find out
who'll be lauded

617
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:43,962
as the best of the year.

618
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:46,840
[camera shutters clicking]

619
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:49,926
[thrilling music continues]

620
00:33:01,188 --> 00:33:02,481
My dates tonight.

621
00:33:02,564 --> 00:33:03,773
Because I'm relevant.

622
00:33:03,857 --> 00:33:05,358
[laughs]

623
00:33:09,779 --> 00:33:11,406
#SSAMAZING

624
00:33:13,909 --> 00:33:16,620
You're here early. What a shock.

625
00:33:16,703 --> 00:33:17,913
Did you sleep here?

626
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:19,498
And why were you late?

627
00:33:19,581 --> 00:33:22,000
Struggled fitting in your girdle?

628
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:24,044
You are both nominated
for Best Actress

629
00:33:24,127 --> 00:33:25,253
how do you feel about that?

630
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:27,589
I wish my dear friend here good luck.

631
00:33:29,466 --> 00:33:31,510
[in English]
May the best actress win.

632
00:33:31,593 --> 00:33:34,262
[reporters cheer, laugh]

633
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:45,190
I want to introduce you all
to our newest artist, Sofie Lasola.

634
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:52,781
- You're really a celebrity now!
- [Sofie] Oh, my god!

635
00:33:52,864 --> 00:33:54,699
- I'm proud of you!
- [Andrea] Sofie, you're so pretty.

636
00:33:54,783 --> 00:33:56,409
Thank you so much, Ms. Andrea!

637
00:33:56,493 --> 00:33:58,954
I didn't expect so many people.

638
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:01,164
It'll be a while before this starts.

639
00:34:01,248 --> 00:34:03,124
- Go socialize.
- [Andrea] Yeah, go and have fun!

640
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,626
- Go!
- Let's go see the band.

641
00:34:04,709 --> 00:34:06,336
- Coming through.
- Chin, let's go.

642
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:12,467
[Noemi] Chin, let's go!

643
00:34:13,677 --> 00:34:16,263
[lively music]

644
00:34:16,346 --> 00:34:17,347
Hi, guys!

645
00:34:24,563 --> 00:34:26,189
One gin and tonic, please.

646
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:30,485
Excuse me.

647
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:33,029
Wait for your turn.

648
00:34:33,655 --> 00:34:35,365
Hey, where's my gin and tonic?
I've been waiting...

649
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:36,783
Can't you just...

650
00:34:37,450 --> 00:34:40,662
Gin and tonic, no ice,
with a slice of lemon.

651
00:34:41,538 --> 00:34:43,540
[giggles]

652
00:34:45,041 --> 00:34:46,418
I really want this to work.

653
00:34:49,296 --> 00:34:50,463
I do too.

654
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:52,257
Let's make it work.

655
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:56,469
♪ Don't ♪

656
00:34:56,553 --> 00:34:59,264
♪ Don't be startled ♪

657
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:01,141
[keyboard clacking]

658
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:03,435
I talked to one of your talents.

659
00:35:03,518 --> 00:35:05,562
They're so happy with your work!

660
00:35:05,937 --> 00:35:07,897
- And the way you use social media...
- Yeah

661
00:35:07,981 --> 00:35:09,190
...Shine is doing work!

662
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:11,067
Remember, I told you before

663
00:35:11,151 --> 00:35:14,154
that there's a project out there
that's totally fit for you.

664
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:17,157
I know you guys are really not afraid
to take on challenges.

665
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,700
You think this will work?

666
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:20,118
Of course it will work!

667
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:23,121
Call us. You're welcome
to join us anytime.

668
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:27,500
Well, my plan is to run for mayor.
If I'm lucky, that is.

669
00:35:27,584 --> 00:35:29,377
Who would you like to team up with?

670
00:35:29,461 --> 00:35:31,546
- Bojack!
- [Monsour] He's here!

671
00:35:31,630 --> 00:35:32,964
[reporter] I'm so shocked!

672
00:35:33,715 --> 00:35:34,716
Boom!

673
00:35:35,008 --> 00:35:37,135
- You all know Niño Muhlach, right?
- Of course, yes!

674
00:35:37,218 --> 00:35:38,928
[Monsour] This is our new tandem.

675
00:35:39,012 --> 00:35:40,472
Mon and Niño.

676
00:35:42,223 --> 00:35:43,600
MonNiño!

677
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:45,894
VOTE! BRAVE, DEPENDABLE,
AND NO-NONSENSE!

678
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:47,437
Thank you!

679
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:49,272
- [reporter] Mother Aleta, over here.
- Over here?

680
00:35:49,356 --> 00:35:50,690
Mother Aleta, look over here, please.

681
00:35:50,774 --> 00:35:51,775
Okay.

682
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:53,610
Mother Aleta!

683
00:35:56,446 --> 00:35:57,447
Mother!

684
00:35:57,864 --> 00:35:59,949
If you'll excuse us. Thanks.

685
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:03,119
Thank you, Matthew. Thank you.

686
00:36:03,620 --> 00:36:04,829
SAM has been sold.

687
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:07,499
I just don't know yet who bought it.

688
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:10,877
5What now?

689
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,837
For all we know, as early as Monday

690
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:14,464
we'll have a new boss.

691
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:16,591
What would you like to drink?

692
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:18,843
Nothing. I want to go inside.

693
00:36:18,927 --> 00:36:20,387
But it hasn't started yet.

694
00:36:20,470 --> 00:36:23,139
No, but it will.

695
00:36:23,223 --> 00:36:24,683
No need to accompany me.

696
00:36:25,350 --> 00:36:26,685
You can sit with us at SAM's table.

697
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:29,479
No, thanks.

698
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:31,147
That's too far from the stage.

699
00:36:31,439 --> 00:36:32,440
I'll see you.

700
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:35,652
[upbeat music]

701
00:36:38,488 --> 00:36:41,032
It's the first time we're attending
an event like this without Samuel.

702
00:36:41,116 --> 00:36:43,702
I know. I wonder
what he'll say if he can see us.

703
00:36:43,785 --> 00:36:45,662
He'll scold us for sure.

704
00:36:46,121 --> 00:36:47,122
No doubt.

705
00:36:48,623 --> 00:36:51,251
But for me, one thing's for sure.

706
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:53,628
I'm very proud of this team.

707
00:36:53,712 --> 00:36:55,296
Oh, yeah. Definitely.

708
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:56,881
And I'm sure Samuel is too.

709
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:01,720
We're SAM. We'll be all right.

710
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:05,306
- Hi, sir!
- Hi, Christian! How are you?

711
00:37:06,182 --> 00:37:07,308
[announcer] Good evening!

712
00:37:08,518 --> 00:37:09,644
[Matthew] Joel!

713
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:11,187
Welcome to this year's
Screen Spirit Awards.

714
00:37:11,271 --> 00:37:12,522
How are you?

715
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:16,067
Here are your hosts

716
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:20,488
Karylle and Robi Domingo!

717
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,202
[grandiose music]

718
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:34,335
[in English] Good evening, everyone!

719
00:37:34,419 --> 00:37:36,713
Whoo! [chuckles]

720
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:41,342
I'm Karylle, and together
with my wonderful co-host, Robi

721
00:37:41,843 --> 00:37:45,305
we are here to welcome you
to the grandest night

722
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:47,599
of Philippine entertainment.

723
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:52,270
- This is the Screen Spirit Awards!
- Screen Spirit Awards!

724
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:54,063
[Robi] Here we go!

725
00:37:54,147 --> 00:37:56,608
[traditional Filipino music]

726
00:38:09,204 --> 00:38:12,040
- Ms. Andrea, we'll be right back...
- Okay.

727
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:19,464
[in Filipino]
This program is insanely long.

728
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:23,718
That's because
we're not winning any awards.

729
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:25,386
[giggles]

730
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:26,471
Whatever.

731
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:29,307
I'll just go to the bathroom, okay?

732
00:38:34,687 --> 00:38:37,023
- [gasps]
- [chuckles]

733
00:38:37,982 --> 00:38:41,611
[in English] So, you decided
to join the sinking ship?

734
00:38:42,737 --> 00:38:45,782
[in Filipino]
Well, it wasn't a difficult decision.

735
00:38:45,865 --> 00:38:47,659
For sure, especially for your kind.

736
00:38:49,786 --> 00:38:50,787
My kind?

737
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:55,375
Those who never use their brains
and think with their hearts instead.

738
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:56,918
You know.

739
00:38:57,377 --> 00:38:58,419
Those...

740
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:00,255
stupid divas!

741
00:39:03,967 --> 00:39:05,051
[door closes]

742
00:39:05,802 --> 00:39:07,554
Goodness gracious.

743
00:39:07,637 --> 00:39:09,013
This jerk.

744
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:10,932
Where have you been?

745
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:12,851
- I was in the bathroom.
- Oh, come on!

746
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:16,145
No regard for other people.

747
00:39:16,980 --> 00:39:17,981
Oh, okay!

748
00:39:18,231 --> 00:39:20,984
[in English] And our Bright Star
of the evening is...

749
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:25,530
[Robi] Ms. Maricel Soriano!

750
00:39:27,699 --> 00:39:28,700
So beautiful.

751
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:32,370
You know, Bright Star is synonymous
with the Diamond Star.

752
00:39:32,453 --> 00:39:34,998
- [Karylle] With a beautiful sash!
- [Robi] Yeah.

753
00:39:35,081 --> 00:39:36,499
What does she get?

754
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:38,001
Here it is!

755
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:39,502
Tonight's Bright Star gets

756
00:39:39,586 --> 00:39:43,423
a year's supply
of Bright Cooking Oil!

757
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:45,091
- Wow!
- [audience applauds]

758
00:39:45,174 --> 00:39:46,926
- [Karylle] Give her a big hand!
- [Hector] Hey, Pops!

759
00:39:47,010 --> 00:39:48,177
Hey, Hec!

760
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:50,096
[in Filipino] You're still here.

761
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:51,723
You should've joined us earlier.

762
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:53,808
It's fine, we had to pack our gear.

763
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,351
[Robi] Ms. Maricel Soriano!

764
00:39:59,731 --> 00:40:01,441
[in English] Hec, I'm sorry.

765
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:06,446
You know what, Pops? It's okay.

766
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:09,198
Seriously, it happened
before we were born.

767
00:40:09,824 --> 00:40:11,576
[in Filipino]
Camille and I are fine with it.

768
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:13,786
[Hector] And actually,
I like her a lot.

769
00:40:14,704 --> 00:40:17,165
It's all good now.
And besides, you're in show business.

770
00:40:17,707 --> 00:40:19,584
Those kinds of dramas are normal.

771
00:40:22,462 --> 00:40:23,713
Your mom's still angry?

772
00:40:24,923 --> 00:40:26,215
I'm sure you understand, Pops.

773
00:40:26,299 --> 00:40:28,426
[Robi in English]
Actually, we are not yet done

774
00:40:28,509 --> 00:40:32,013
because we got our last special award
for the evening

775
00:40:32,096 --> 00:40:34,474
and that is our Sparkling Star
of the night

776
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:38,144
and that person is none other than...

777
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:41,522
Ms. Snooky Serna!

778
00:40:42,231 --> 00:40:44,233
[crowd cheering]

779
00:40:44,817 --> 00:40:46,319
[Karylle] Also looking great

780
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:48,905
in her black ensemble, with a fringe!

781
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:52,325
[in Filipino] Matching her tattoos.

782
00:40:52,408 --> 00:40:53,534
Bright and Sparkle.

783
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:55,662
Here is her award.

784
00:40:55,745 --> 00:40:57,080
[in English] Congratulations.

785
00:40:57,163 --> 00:40:59,165
Our Sparkling Star of the night gets

786
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:03,294
a year's supply
of Sparkle Laundry Bar!

787
00:41:03,378 --> 00:41:05,463
- [Robi] Wow!
- I need to approve the script.

788
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:07,548
I don't want them sneaking
an endorsement into my lines.

789
00:41:07,632 --> 00:41:09,008
I don't do that.

790
00:41:09,092 --> 00:41:11,761
No way. What are you waiting for?

791
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:14,555
I'm next and I need my lines!

792
00:41:15,056 --> 00:41:18,768
- Amateurs!
- Sir Dick, hello, I'm Chin.

793
00:41:18,851 --> 00:41:20,436
- Chin?
- From SAM.

794
00:41:21,145 --> 00:41:23,773
We are presenting
this Lifetime Achievement Award

795
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:27,443
to commemorate a legendary actress
of the film industry.

796
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:30,947
She starred in her first film
during the 1920s

797
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:35,910
Serene Maiden, that gave her
the nickname "Maria Clara."

798
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,746
Are you sure you're not gonna come?

799
00:41:40,415 --> 00:41:42,959
It's okay if you arrive late.

800
00:41:43,626 --> 00:41:46,004
[Zsa Zsa over phone]
No, honey, I'm too embarrassed.

801
00:41:46,379 --> 00:41:49,549
They'll ask about my drunken stream.

802
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:51,551
They've all forgotten about that.

803
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:53,553
By the time I get there

804
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:55,346
you'll be done anyway.

805
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:57,765
I can just get a copy.

806
00:41:58,391 --> 00:42:00,018
We'll watch it together.

807
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:02,478
Okay, yeah.

808
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:06,190
Love you. Okay. Bye, Mama.

809
00:42:07,734 --> 00:42:10,987
Ms. Encarnacion Dimamatay.

810
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:34,427
♪ Late at night ♪

811
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:37,847
♪ Looking at the stars ♪

812
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:41,726
♪ I'm thinking of you, baby ♪

813
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:44,854
♪ Wondering where you are ♪

814
00:42:44,937 --> 00:42:48,858
♪ When I say good night ♪

815
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:51,736
♪ Turn out the lights ♪

816
00:42:51,819 --> 00:42:55,865
♪ I still lay awake,
Dreaming of you ♪

817
00:42:55,948 --> 00:43:01,120
♪ Holding me tight ♪

818
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:09,045
- ♪ Starlight, star bright
- Starlight, star bright ♪

819
00:43:09,128 --> 00:43:12,965
- ♪ Wish I may...
- Wish I may, wish I might ♪

820
00:43:13,049 --> 00:43:15,802
♪ Won't you make him love me too? ♪

821
00:43:15,885 --> 00:43:19,514
♪ Make him want to hold me too ♪

822
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:22,683
♪ And wish upon a star ♪

823
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:28,815
♪ As I do ♪

824
00:43:29,357 --> 00:43:31,317
Ladies and gentlemen

825
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:34,779
my legendary mother,
Ms. Zsa Zsa Padilla.

826
00:43:35,113 --> 00:43:37,490
My daughter, Karylle.

827
00:43:39,200 --> 00:43:40,952
♪ I'll never stop ♪

828
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:43,037
♪ Wishing on that star ♪

829
00:43:43,121 --> 00:43:46,165
♪ I'll never stop wishing ♪

830
00:43:46,249 --> 00:43:49,669
- ♪ Till my dreams come true
- Till my dreams come true ♪

831
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:53,089
- ♪ And I can hold you
- And I can hold you ♪

832
00:43:53,172 --> 00:43:58,010
- ♪ And love you
- And love you ♪

833
00:43:58,094 --> 00:44:01,347
- ♪ Make him want to hold me too
- Make him want to hold me too ♪

834
00:44:01,430 --> 00:44:05,059
- ♪ And promise me forever
- And promise me forever ♪

835
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:09,605
- ♪ And wish upon a star
- And wish upon a star ♪

836
00:44:09,689 --> 00:44:12,441
♪ I'm wishing on starlight ♪

837
00:44:12,525 --> 00:44:17,155
♪ Wishing on starlight ♪

838
00:44:18,406 --> 00:44:23,619
- ♪ Star bright
- Star bright ♪

839
00:44:24,036 --> 00:44:26,455
- Go!
- [cheering]

840
00:44:29,292 --> 00:44:32,003
[in unison]
And the 69th Screen Spirit Award

841
00:44:32,086 --> 00:44:34,255
for Best Actor goes to...

842
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:36,382
[Maricel] Rod... [coughs]

843
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:38,092
...Paulate, The Lonely One.

844
00:44:38,176 --> 00:44:40,261
[crowd applauding]

845
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:46,350
[Roderick] Thank you so much.

846
00:44:46,893 --> 00:44:48,019
How many of these have I gotten?

847
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:50,104
I've gotten a lot.

848
00:44:50,897 --> 00:44:55,359
When I heard my name called for this

849
00:44:55,443 --> 00:44:57,653
I remembered when I was just 19.

850
00:44:57,737 --> 00:45:01,782
I just wanted to be seen
on television, movies.

851
00:45:02,366 --> 00:45:04,911
- That's it. That was my dream.
- We should go.

852
00:45:04,994 --> 00:45:06,746
- But you know...
- We'll go slowly.

853
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:08,915
I was just a newbie
in the field of acting.

854
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:13,169
Yet right off the bat,
I won two awards, just like that!

855
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:16,047
I told myself,
"You are really blessed."

856
00:45:16,130 --> 00:45:17,798
And when I was 22

857
00:45:17,882 --> 00:45:21,427
I wanted to give the audience
what they wanted.

858
00:45:21,510 --> 00:45:24,180
Hello, hello there!
Now, I've worked with these ladies.

859
00:45:24,388 --> 00:45:27,600
These two right here onstage.

860
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:29,894
I've worked with them
in some of my films.

861
00:45:29,977 --> 00:45:33,231
But as for the awards,
they weren't as fortunate as me.

862
00:45:33,314 --> 00:45:34,732
I always end up with the awards.

863
00:45:34,815 --> 00:45:36,734
But I'm not one to brag.

864
00:45:37,109 --> 00:45:40,863
When I was younger...
So when I was 22 years old...

865
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:45,326
...and do anything
to entertain audiences...

866
00:45:45,409 --> 00:45:49,497
...so I was 15, and even at school

867
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:51,040
I kept getting the awards.

868
00:45:51,499 --> 00:45:52,500
We should go.

869
00:45:52,583 --> 00:45:53,876
My legs are getting numb.

870
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:56,003
I won't take any more of your time.

871
00:45:56,087 --> 00:45:58,839
When I was a child,
our house would always get flooded.

872
00:45:59,507 --> 00:46:01,759
That was hard for me as a kid.

873
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:03,261
The directors would even ask me

874
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:05,304
"How do you make your...

875
00:46:05,388 --> 00:46:07,890
while you're on camera,
when we're about to start

876
00:46:07,974 --> 00:46:09,558
you haven't spoken a single line

877
00:46:09,642 --> 00:46:11,352
teardrops roll down right on cue?"

878
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:13,562
That's how blessings work sometimes.

879
00:46:13,646 --> 00:46:16,023
This is my 18th Best Actor award!

880
00:46:16,107 --> 00:46:18,985
Let's hear it for me! [laughs]

881
00:46:20,278 --> 00:46:21,904
Eighteen awards!

882
00:46:21,988 --> 00:46:26,575
Now I'd have to remodel my house
to make space for this new award.

883
00:46:26,659 --> 00:46:29,745
That's the downside
of getting awards.

884
00:46:29,829 --> 00:46:31,622
The nerve of that man.

885
00:46:32,206 --> 00:46:34,834
- Right?
- Define audacious.

886
00:46:35,751 --> 00:46:41,215
So I would like to thank
this award-giving body.

887
00:46:41,924 --> 00:46:43,843
And of course, how can I forget?

888
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:46,595
I want to thank you...

889
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,015
Paul Amir!

890
00:46:49,098 --> 00:46:51,517
Thank you so much.

891
00:46:52,435 --> 00:46:54,812
Thirty percent of my gratitude

892
00:46:54,895 --> 00:46:58,607
and thirty percent
of my salary goes to you.

893
00:47:00,109 --> 00:47:01,652
But not anymore.

894
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:03,362
- What was that?
- That's all.

895
00:47:03,446 --> 00:47:06,449
I wasn't too prepared.
I'm sorry for my quick speech.

896
00:47:06,532 --> 00:47:07,700
Thank you.

897
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:09,744
- [gasps]
- I like this.

898
00:47:09,827 --> 00:47:12,788
[announcer] Let's give it up
for the national champions!

899
00:47:12,872 --> 00:47:14,332
NU Pep Squad!

900
00:47:14,415 --> 00:47:18,085
[upbeat music]

901
00:47:22,757 --> 00:47:26,260
- Congratulations, sir.
- [Roderick] Thank you!

902
00:47:26,344 --> 00:47:28,220
Roderick, excuse me.

903
00:47:29,138 --> 00:47:31,640
What happened there? I mean...

904
00:47:32,141 --> 00:47:33,225
You see this?

905
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:35,895
I'll let you in on a secret...

906
00:47:36,270 --> 00:47:38,481
- What is it?
- Paul Amir told me that...

907
00:47:42,026 --> 00:47:44,487
Now, call me a stupid diva.

908
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:46,947
- Wait a minute.
- We're done!

909
00:47:48,157 --> 00:47:49,158
Or I'll knock you out.

910
00:47:53,621 --> 00:47:55,998
[upbeat music]

911
00:48:06,634 --> 00:48:08,344
You played me for a fool!

912
00:48:13,849 --> 00:48:14,850
Hi, Paul.

913
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:20,231
I've done that to a lot of people.

914
00:48:21,982 --> 00:48:23,025
[in English] Let me remind you

915
00:48:23,109 --> 00:48:25,236
that I still have the documents
that you gave me.

916
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:27,363
[in Filipino]
Your talents won't be happy

917
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:30,574
when they find out
you're giving away their secrets.

918
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:32,535
Paul, if I were you

919
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:33,869
I'd burn those phony papers.

920
00:48:33,953 --> 00:48:36,330
[in English] There's no truth
in any of those documents.

921
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:41,001
[in Filipino]
So it was all part of your grand plan

922
00:48:41,460 --> 00:48:45,256
for me to retract my offer
to make Helen mad.

923
00:48:47,466 --> 00:48:48,968
I needed to buy some time.

924
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:50,302
At my expense.

925
00:48:50,719 --> 00:48:52,304
So look what happened.

926
00:48:52,680 --> 00:48:56,475
We both missed out on SAM.

927
00:48:58,227 --> 00:49:00,187
What, you didn't get SAM?

928
00:49:00,271 --> 00:49:02,189
How could that happen

929
00:49:02,273 --> 00:49:04,650
when Helen's really mad at me
for retracting my offer?

930
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:13,409
[Matthew] I didn't get it.
You didn't get it.

931
00:49:14,452 --> 00:49:15,453
So who did?

932
00:49:15,744 --> 00:49:17,746
[grandiose music]

933
00:49:19,457 --> 00:49:22,418
[announcer] The nominees
for Best Actress are...

934
00:49:25,337 --> 00:49:26,922
I think I know who bought SAM.

935
00:49:28,132 --> 00:49:29,133
Who?

936
00:49:35,598 --> 00:49:39,768
Lynette Marie Vicencio, Amihan and I.

937
00:49:40,811 --> 00:49:44,440
Lotlot de Leon, The Sacrifice.

938
00:49:44,523 --> 00:49:46,108
- Frank?
- Frank?

939
00:49:58,204 --> 00:50:01,207
Maricel Soriano, For Alida.

940
00:50:05,336 --> 00:50:08,756
Snooky Serna, Sabel's Secret.

941
00:50:12,343 --> 00:50:15,346
This year's Best Actress is...

942
00:50:17,973 --> 00:50:19,850
Lynette Marie Vicencio

943
00:50:20,809 --> 00:50:22,728
Amihan and I.

944
00:50:29,360 --> 00:50:30,444
What the heck?

945
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,905
This is truly shocking.

946
00:50:32,988 --> 00:50:35,407
I'm so shocked. What a shocker!

947
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:38,536
Thank you!

948
00:50:39,411 --> 00:50:40,412
Thank you!

949
00:50:50,673 --> 00:50:53,592
The Best Picture award goes to

950
00:50:53,676 --> 00:50:56,303
The Offering by Royal Lion Films.

951
00:50:56,387 --> 00:51:01,725
To all the staff and crew
of Royal Lion

952
00:51:01,809 --> 00:51:04,061
who have been working
with me for a long time

953
00:51:04,144 --> 00:51:06,647
to The Offering's director

954
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:08,857
Cyrus Mariveles

955
00:51:08,941 --> 00:51:11,485
and to my superb cast

956
00:51:11,569 --> 00:51:14,029
headed by Ms. Lotlot De Leon

957
00:51:14,113 --> 00:51:17,700
thank you so much to all of you.

958
00:51:19,201 --> 00:51:22,454
I've been in this industry
for a long time.

959
00:51:24,540 --> 00:51:26,333
And even though

960
00:51:28,002 --> 00:51:30,296
the time may be nearing

961
00:51:30,838 --> 00:51:32,548
when I won't be here anymore...

962
00:51:35,384 --> 00:51:39,346
[Aleta] I believe
I have beautiful things

963
00:51:39,430 --> 00:51:42,474
I could leave behind for all of you.

964
00:51:44,518 --> 00:51:47,896
I introduced a lot of trends,
love teams

965
00:51:49,273 --> 00:51:52,109
sexy flicks, action movies

966
00:51:52,192 --> 00:51:55,404
family dramas, and more.

967
00:51:57,448 --> 00:51:59,491
But in everything I've done

968
00:52:00,367 --> 00:52:02,828
I've tried to keep

969
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:05,748
our showbiz world lively and vibrant.

970
00:52:06,749 --> 00:52:09,251
Because I truly love this world.

971
00:52:13,255 --> 00:52:19,094
Even though we've faced
more losses than wins

972
00:52:19,178 --> 00:52:22,931
I'm still here. We're still here.

973
00:52:23,349 --> 00:52:25,976
[crowd applauding]

974
00:52:28,937 --> 00:52:31,106
So I express my gratitude

975
00:52:32,066 --> 00:52:33,984
to those people

976
00:52:34,068 --> 00:52:36,862
who tirelessly give their love

977
00:52:36,945 --> 00:52:39,073
and care to this industry.

978
00:52:40,449 --> 00:52:42,326
Even though many think

979
00:52:44,161 --> 00:52:46,038
we're already obsolete.

980
00:52:48,666 --> 00:52:51,210
[somber music]

981
00:53:04,515 --> 00:53:06,392
Thank you all.

982
00:53:06,975 --> 00:53:07,976
Thank you!

983
00:53:08,060 --> 00:53:09,728
- We love you, Mother!
- [Aleta] Thank you!

984
00:53:09,812 --> 00:53:10,813
[Andrea] Mother!

985
00:53:12,439 --> 00:53:15,234
- We love you, Mother!
- Love you, Mother!

986
00:53:15,317 --> 00:53:17,069
[Gab] Love you, Mother!

987
00:53:32,126 --> 00:53:34,044
[in English]
Dick, congratulations again.

988
00:53:34,128 --> 00:53:35,212
You deserve it!

989
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:37,464
[Roderick in Filipino] Thank you!
Another Best Actor award!

990
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:39,550
- [Andrea] I know!
- [Roderick] Thank you.

991
00:53:41,343 --> 00:53:42,678
- Thank you.
- [Andrea] Bye!

992
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:45,180
- Many more!
- Congratulations!

993
00:53:47,599 --> 00:53:49,351
Mary. Good night.

994
00:53:49,435 --> 00:53:51,145
- Good night.
- I'll give you a call.

995
00:53:51,228 --> 00:53:53,814
- Thank you again for coming.
- Okay.

996
00:53:54,565 --> 00:53:55,566
Bye!

997
00:53:55,816 --> 00:53:56,817
Bye-bye!

998
00:53:57,985 --> 00:53:59,445
Bye!

999
00:53:59,528 --> 00:54:00,571
[sighs]

1000
00:54:01,905 --> 00:54:03,907
Well, what do you think?

1001
00:54:05,159 --> 00:54:06,160
About?

1002
00:54:06,535 --> 00:54:09,079
Would Maricel and Snooky take it well

1003
00:54:09,997 --> 00:54:11,957
if we put Roderick on SAM's roster?

1004
00:54:12,583 --> 00:54:15,836
That is, if we still have
a SAM roster to put him on.

1005
00:54:15,919 --> 00:54:18,172
Guys, did you get this?

1006
00:54:18,255 --> 00:54:20,424
- It's Mother Aleta.
- Mother Aleta.

1007
00:54:20,507 --> 00:54:21,717
Didn't you get a message?

1008
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:22,801
- Go check.
- [Noemi] Why?

1009
00:54:23,510 --> 00:54:24,511
What?

1010
00:54:29,016 --> 00:54:30,768
[line ringing]

1011
00:54:30,851 --> 00:54:33,479
[Andrea] Noemi, let's go! Hurry up!

1012
00:54:33,562 --> 00:54:35,564
Mother's not picking up.

1013
00:54:35,647 --> 00:54:38,817
Margie texted, Mother's at home.

1014
00:54:38,901 --> 00:54:41,153
Home? Why didn't they bring her
to the hospital?

1015
00:54:41,236 --> 00:54:44,907
Right. It should be a hospital first,
then the morgue. That's protocol.

1016
00:54:44,990 --> 00:54:47,075
- Chin!
- What morgue?

1017
00:54:47,576 --> 00:54:48,952
Didn't you hear her speech?

1018
00:54:49,036 --> 00:54:50,496
It's like she was saying
her farewell.

1019
00:54:50,579 --> 00:54:52,915
As if she's about to die.
What do we do?

1020
00:54:52,998 --> 00:54:54,792
[Gab] Chin, shut up!

1021
00:54:54,875 --> 00:54:57,586
[tense music]

1022
00:55:04,551 --> 00:55:08,138
- Mother?
- Mother?

1023
00:55:13,101 --> 00:55:14,102
[Gab] Mother!

1024
00:55:14,478 --> 00:55:16,647
- [Andrea] Mother!
- [Chin] Mother!

1025
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:18,106
- Mother!
- What's happening?

1026
00:55:18,190 --> 00:55:19,441
[Andrea] Mother! Oh, god!

1027
00:55:19,525 --> 00:55:22,194
- Mother?
- I was afraid this would happen.

1028
00:55:22,277 --> 00:55:24,863
- Mother.
- Oh, my god, Mother!

1029
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:26,365
What should we do?

1030
00:55:26,782 --> 00:55:27,991
What... I don't know.

1031
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:31,370
[glasses clinking]

1032
00:55:34,206 --> 00:55:36,416
Ma'am, here's your coffee.

1033
00:55:36,750 --> 00:55:38,126
[mumbles]

1034
00:55:38,210 --> 00:55:40,921
- [Gab] Mother?
- Fix me a cup.

1035
00:55:41,004 --> 00:55:44,216
Mother! Oh, my god!

1036
00:55:44,299 --> 00:55:45,425
Hm?

1037
00:55:45,509 --> 00:55:46,844
Mother, what happened?

1038
00:55:46,927 --> 00:55:48,011
Hm?

1039
00:55:48,095 --> 00:55:50,889
You texted me saying
something happened.

1040
00:55:52,140 --> 00:55:54,226
SAM X MOTHER ALETA
SOMETHING HAPPENED...

1041
00:55:54,309 --> 00:55:58,146
Well, it was clear when I wrote that.

1042
00:55:58,438 --> 00:56:00,357
[giggles]

1043
00:56:00,774 --> 00:56:03,610
Mother, tell us what happened.

1044
00:56:05,153 --> 00:56:09,491
They gave me a drink backstage

1045
00:56:09,575 --> 00:56:12,035
because I won.

1046
00:56:12,870 --> 00:56:14,538
I stumbled.

1047
00:56:15,622 --> 00:56:16,957
And you threw up!

1048
00:56:17,249 --> 00:56:18,667
No, I threw up.

1049
00:56:20,586 --> 00:56:22,045
Why is everyone here?

1050
00:56:22,421 --> 00:56:25,591
I called you here just to chat.

1051
00:56:25,674 --> 00:56:28,635
Why would I kill myself? Lunatics.

1052
00:56:28,719 --> 00:56:30,554
[Gab] It's Chin's fault, Mother.

1053
00:56:31,179 --> 00:56:35,350
After all I've been through,
I'd commit suicide?

1054
00:56:35,434 --> 00:56:36,518
No.

1055
00:56:36,852 --> 00:56:39,479
- I don't want that.
- You're so stubborn.

1056
00:56:39,563 --> 00:56:42,608
Well, Mother,
maybe it's us who should be

1057
00:56:42,691 --> 00:56:44,276
thinking of ending things.

1058
00:56:44,359 --> 00:56:47,029
[Andrea] Give us some of those pills,
that'll do the job.

1059
00:56:47,112 --> 00:56:49,114
- [Matthew] Hey, guys. Hey.
- They're right there.

1060
00:56:49,197 --> 00:56:52,534
Remember that Helen sold SAM.

1061
00:56:53,702 --> 00:56:55,913
Most likely by Monday...

1062
00:56:57,497 --> 00:57:00,375
Frank Villacin will be our new boss.

1063
00:57:00,459 --> 00:57:01,710
Good God.

1064
00:57:03,337 --> 00:57:05,589
Have you told the kids?

1065
00:57:06,590 --> 00:57:08,467
They've told us, Mother.

1066
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:11,428
That's why we raided
your wine cabinet.

1067
00:57:12,429 --> 00:57:16,099
These are meant for guests,
since you don't really drink, right?

1068
00:57:16,558 --> 00:57:18,560
Well, you already helped yourselves.

1069
00:57:20,187 --> 00:57:22,898
[clicks tongue] So what's the plan?

1070
00:57:22,981 --> 00:57:24,858
What else,
except to switch to Galaxy?

1071
00:57:24,942 --> 00:57:26,234
- [Camille] Yuck!
- [Sofie] Eww!

1072
00:57:27,110 --> 00:57:28,820
Eww, Galaxy?

1073
00:57:28,904 --> 00:57:30,072
Which do you prefer...

1074
00:57:30,822 --> 00:57:32,449
- Paul Amir?
- A big jerk.

1075
00:57:33,492 --> 00:57:35,452
- Frank Villacin?
- Another jerk.

1076
00:57:35,535 --> 00:57:37,120
[Noemi] Maybe I'll be
a domestic helper.

1077
00:57:37,204 --> 00:57:38,956
- [Chin] Me too.
- [Camille] I'll go home to Baguio.

1078
00:57:39,039 --> 00:57:40,582
Wait. In the meantime...

1079
00:57:44,044 --> 00:57:45,045
Let's toast to Noemi

1080
00:57:46,046 --> 00:57:47,839
our newest manager.

1081
00:57:47,923 --> 00:57:51,009
And the last! Cheers!

1082
00:57:52,094 --> 00:57:53,637
- [Camille] Cheers to that!
- Thank you.

1083
00:57:54,179 --> 00:57:55,305
[Noemi] That's harsh, Chin.

1084
00:57:55,389 --> 00:57:58,141
The most unfortunate one is Camille.

1085
00:57:58,225 --> 00:58:01,687
She's new and now she lost her job.

1086
00:58:01,770 --> 00:58:04,564
Yeah, just when she's getting used to
working for Andrea.

1087
00:58:05,273 --> 00:58:07,192
- What do you mean by that?
- [Camille] No, to be honest

1088
00:58:07,275 --> 00:58:09,987
I'm more afraid of Chin and Noemi now
than I am of Ms. Andrea.

1089
00:58:10,070 --> 00:58:13,156
Bully. Bigger bully. Biggest bully.

1090
00:58:13,573 --> 00:58:16,118
- What are you trying to say?
- [Chin] Just kidding.

1091
00:58:19,246 --> 00:58:21,289
Let's not forget to congratulate...

1092
00:58:22,249 --> 00:58:24,042
- Mother Aleta.
- Hm?

1093
00:58:24,126 --> 00:58:26,878
You deserve that award,
you really do.

1094
00:58:26,962 --> 00:58:28,505
Thank you, thank you!

1095
00:58:28,588 --> 00:58:32,843
My film only won
because they're all afraid of me.

1096
00:58:32,926 --> 00:58:34,803
[all laugh]

1097
00:58:34,886 --> 00:58:36,638
- But still, cheers to that!
- Cheers!

1098
00:58:36,722 --> 00:58:39,307
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

1099
00:58:39,391 --> 00:58:41,268
Cheers! Except you.

1100
00:58:44,021 --> 00:58:45,772
But, Mother...

1101
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:48,316
what's going to happen to us?

1102
00:58:51,111 --> 00:58:53,655
[tense music]

1103
00:58:53,739 --> 00:58:55,949
- [server] Mother, this is for you.
- Okay.

1104
00:58:56,783 --> 00:58:57,784
Thank you.

1105
00:59:17,512 --> 00:59:18,513
[Aleta] Thank you.

1106
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:24,561
[tense music continues]

1107
00:59:31,234 --> 00:59:32,694
[Gab] Let me see that.

1108
00:59:33,278 --> 00:59:34,279
[Matthew] Excuse me.

1109
00:59:37,032 --> 00:59:38,158
[Andrea] Give me that.

1110
00:59:39,367 --> 00:59:41,286
Fifty percent to Mother Aleta

1111
00:59:41,369 --> 00:59:42,954
50 percent split among you three.

1112
00:59:43,455 --> 00:59:45,665
So that means you all own SAM?

1113
00:59:45,749 --> 00:59:48,001
Oh, shoot, now I've sobered up.

1114
00:59:48,085 --> 00:59:51,088
- Mother? Mother!
- [Aleta] You're welcome!

1115
00:59:51,671 --> 00:59:53,381
Oh, oh, oh!

1116
00:59:53,465 --> 00:59:55,717
That's a loan! You have to pay me!

1117
00:59:55,801 --> 00:59:58,678
Hug me and I'll bill you tomorrow.

1118
00:59:58,762 --> 01:00:00,388
I'll just kiss you.

1119
01:00:00,472 --> 01:00:01,473
[Noemi] Sofie!

1120
01:00:01,556 --> 01:00:03,183
- [Sofie] I still have a manager!
- Mother.

1121
01:00:03,892 --> 01:00:05,143
Uh...

1122
01:00:05,519 --> 01:00:06,561
Cheers.

1123
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:08,647
- [Camille] Cheers!
- [Gab] To Mother Aleta!

1124
01:00:08,730 --> 01:00:11,066
- Cheers, Mother!
- Cheers, Mother!

1125
01:00:11,817 --> 01:00:16,988
Cheers to Shine Artist Management!

1126
01:00:17,072 --> 01:00:18,073
Yay!

1127
01:00:18,156 --> 01:00:21,409
As early as Monday,
we'll rush the office renovations

1128
01:00:21,493 --> 01:00:23,370
so we can set up your new office.

1129
01:00:25,455 --> 01:00:28,166
I don't want to work
in your deteriorating office.

1130
01:00:29,042 --> 01:00:31,378
I'm done managing talents.

1131
01:00:31,711 --> 01:00:35,257
And I'm not holding office at SAM.

1132
01:00:35,340 --> 01:00:36,967
I have my own office.

1133
01:00:37,050 --> 01:00:38,969
I have my own job.

1134
01:00:39,386 --> 01:00:42,305
SAM will be your responsibility.

1135
01:00:42,931 --> 01:00:46,476
So, Mother, who will be our boss?

1136
01:00:46,560 --> 01:00:49,521
Well, I... I want to head SAM.

1137
01:00:50,438 --> 01:00:52,274
I have what it takes, I'm qualified.

1138
01:00:52,357 --> 01:00:53,483
I'm qualified too.

1139
01:00:53,567 --> 01:00:54,651
Me too.

1140
01:00:54,734 --> 01:00:57,320
Well, we all are,
and I have a lot of new ideas.

1141
01:00:58,113 --> 01:00:59,156
[Andrea] What ideas?

1142
01:00:59,239 --> 01:01:01,241
Okay, what do you think, Mother?

1143
01:01:01,950 --> 01:01:03,285
What do I think?

1144
01:01:03,952 --> 01:01:06,830
Why the heck are you all working
on a weekend?

1145
01:01:06,913 --> 01:01:08,165
[Chin] There you go...

1146
01:01:08,248 --> 01:01:11,793
There's a time for all that,
but not tonight.

1147
01:01:12,335 --> 01:01:13,753
Not tomorrow night.

1148
01:01:14,421 --> 01:01:16,214
Maybe on Monday.

1149
01:01:17,215 --> 01:01:19,092
[Aleta] Or the next Monday.

1150
01:01:19,968 --> 01:01:21,469
One of these Mondays.

1151
01:01:23,388 --> 01:01:25,098
[cell phone pings]

1152
01:01:25,599 --> 01:01:27,225
- [Andrea] Wait.
- [Aleta] What's that?

1153
01:01:30,770 --> 01:01:34,107
[Frank] I mentioned before
that the list

1154
01:01:34,191 --> 01:01:38,945
of those tax evaders
was just a partial one.

1155
01:01:39,029 --> 01:01:41,531
I have here with me...

1156
01:01:42,824 --> 01:01:45,619
another list of tax evaders.

1157
01:01:45,702 --> 01:01:49,581
And again, I urge the DIR

1158
01:01:50,916 --> 01:01:53,335
to really go after these tax evaders

1159
01:01:53,418 --> 01:01:56,755
for the sake of the Filipino people.

1160
01:01:57,923 --> 01:02:00,175
"Punch-Punch Crystals.

1161
01:02:01,051 --> 01:02:04,304
Polyver Enterprises.

1162
01:02:05,013 --> 01:02:07,224
Pressman Incorporated.

1163
01:02:07,849 --> 01:02:10,268
Mr. Retivert Yam.

1164
01:02:10,727 --> 01:02:12,854
SStrike Enterprises.

1165
01:02:14,522 --> 01:02:18,151
Shine Artist Management.

1166
01:02:19,694 --> 01:02:22,489
Titular and Associates."

1167
01:02:22,572 --> 01:02:24,449
That's it for now.

1168
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:26,826
- Well...
- [sighs]

1169
01:02:29,037 --> 01:02:34,209
All I can say is,
to whoever will head SAM...

1170
01:02:36,628 --> 01:02:37,629
good luck.

1171
01:02:39,589 --> 01:02:41,258
- Good luck.
- [frustrated sigh]

1172
01:02:42,592 --> 01:02:43,593
Mother.

1173
01:02:50,350 --> 01:02:51,351
[groans]

1174
01:03:03,697 --> 01:03:06,700
I found this in Samuel's office.

1175
01:03:07,450 --> 01:03:10,662
SAM IS ALL OF YOU

1176
01:03:15,917 --> 01:03:17,961
A lot will happen with SAM.

1177
01:03:20,588 --> 01:03:22,299
[Aleta] As early as Monday

1178
01:03:23,133 --> 01:03:25,218
you have to deal with Frank Villacin.

1179
01:03:25,885 --> 01:03:28,596
And if Roderick is going to join you

1180
01:03:28,680 --> 01:03:31,224
you will have to deal
with Paul Amir as well.

1181
01:03:32,851 --> 01:03:35,020
ABS-CBN is closed,
what are you going to do about that?

1182
01:03:37,856 --> 01:03:42,360
The entire industry of movies,
television, all out of sorts.

1183
01:03:42,444 --> 01:03:46,740
The issues are unending,
working conditions, working hours

1184
01:03:47,157 --> 01:03:49,993
intellectual property rights,
there's a lot.

1185
01:03:50,076 --> 01:03:51,119
Even you.

1186
01:03:52,370 --> 01:03:55,332
You have issues
in your personal lives.

1187
01:03:56,041 --> 01:03:58,960
Relationships that need
to be repaired.

1188
01:04:01,588 --> 01:04:05,425
You have talents that rely on you...

1189
01:04:06,134 --> 01:04:07,969
for their livelihood.

1190
01:04:09,971 --> 01:04:11,473
What do these all mean?

1191
01:04:13,683 --> 01:04:17,687
The world is spinning fast,
really fast!

1192
01:04:17,937 --> 01:04:21,483
You all have to go with the flow.

1193
01:04:23,526 --> 01:04:28,698
But never forget why SAM is here.

1194
01:04:32,327 --> 01:04:35,747
Why you keep fighting for SAM.

1195
01:04:55,558 --> 01:04:56,684
[Matthew] You know what I think?

1196
01:04:56,768 --> 01:04:58,186
[Andrea] Save that for Monday.

1197
01:05:00,146 --> 01:05:01,147
Monday.

1198
01:05:01,981 --> 01:05:03,441
Monday, guys, okay?

1199
01:05:05,235 --> 01:05:06,361
[Matthew] Monday it is.

1200
01:05:10,824 --> 01:05:12,242
[mumbles]

1201
01:05:13,827 --> 01:05:16,079
Monday...

1202
01:05:16,287 --> 01:05:19,040
[somber music]

1203
01:05:24,254 --> 01:05:25,922
[Samuel] I used to tell myself...

1204
01:05:26,923 --> 01:05:28,007
"Sam...

1205
01:05:29,175 --> 01:05:31,094
You know that love is hard."

1206
01:05:32,595 --> 01:05:35,432
[in English]
But when it works, it works.

1207
01:05:36,683 --> 01:05:37,934
And it feels good!

1208
01:05:40,520 --> 01:05:44,649
[in Filipino] I wish I could still
be here at the end of this story.

1209
01:05:45,567 --> 01:05:46,860
So I can finally understand

1210
01:05:48,111 --> 01:05:49,571
all the reasons

1211
01:05:51,072 --> 01:05:53,116
behind all my struggles.

